### Explored Factors

#### Dispersion-Conditioned Short-Term Reversal

The candidate combines three-session reversal with a market-wide dispersion regime multiplier:

\[
F_{i,t}
=
-\text{return}_{i,t-3:t}
\times
\operatorname{clip}\left(
\frac{\text{cross-asset dispersion}_{t}}
{\operatorname{median}_{60}(\text{dispersion})},
0.5,2.0
\right)
\]

The signal is shifted by one completed session. Higher values favor assets with weaker recent performance, particularly when cross-asset dispersion is elevated.

