#### Downside Asymmetry Quality

The candidate measures the ratio of average positive daily-return magnitude to average absolute negative daily-return magnitude over the trailing 30 sessions:

\[
F_{i,t}
=
\frac{\operatorname{mean}(\max(r_{i,t-29:t},0))}
{\operatorname{mean}(|\min(r_{i,t-29:t},0)|)+10^{-8}}
\]

The signal is shifted by one completed session. Higher values favor assets exhibiting stronger upside asymmetry and comparatively contained downside moves.

